# seaview.conf
#
# Copy this file to "seaview.conf" (same directory as start-seaview.sh) and
# edit for your machine. Any value can also be overridden on the command
# line, e.g.:
#   ./start-seaview.sh --ip 192.168.2.125 --com COM11
#
# For the ethernet transport, only CONVERTER_IP is required; everything else
# has a working default or is auto-detected.

# Transport:
#   "ethernet" - RS485-to-Ethernet converter, bridged in via socat + tty0tty.
#                This is the FMD deployment architecture.
#   "usb"      - USB serial adapter mapped straight to a Wine COM port.
#                For bench work before the converter is in the loop.
TRANSPORT="ethernet"

# --- ethernet transport ----------------------------------------------------

# IP address of the RS485-to-Ethernet converter
CONVERTER_IP="192.168.2.125"

# TCP port the converter serves RAW serial data on. Many converters expose
# their configuration menu on a different port (often 23) than the raw data
# stream - make sure this is the raw one.
CONVERTER_PORT="2000"

# Which tty0tty pair to use: 0, 2, 4, or 6 (pairs are N <-> N+1).
# Leave blank to auto-detect the first working pair.
TNT_PAIR=""

# --- usb transport ---------------------------------------------------------

# Serial device for TRANSPORT="usb". Leave blank to auto-detect; the script
# prefers /dev/serial/by-id/* because /dev/ttyUSB* renumbers on replug.
USB_PORT=""

# --- common ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Wine COM port name to expose. Select this inside seaView.
WINE_COM_PORT="COM11"

# Windows-style path (as Wine sees it) to seaView.
SEAVIEW_EXE='C:\Program Files\Impact Subsea\seaView\seaView.exe'

# Wine prefix. MUST be 64-bit - seaView.exe is a 64-bit binary and a win32
# prefix rejects it with "Bad EXE format". Leave blank to use $WINEPREFIX
# from the environment, or ~/.wine-seaview if that is also unset.
#
# Note this deliberately does NOT default to ~/.wine, which is 32-bit on a
# stock Ubuntu install.
WINEPREFIX=""

# Only needed if the tty0tty module is not already installed system-wide.
# Leave blank to use the location install-tty0tty.sh stages it into:
#   ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/tty0tty/module
TTY0TTY_DIR=""
